# The general rule first: later patterns win in this file, so anything
# meant to override has to come after it. Normalise in the repository,
# check out with LF, so sources do not acquire carriage returns on a
# Windows clone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# And the exceptions. The corpus is compared byte for byte and the
# round-trip promise is about bytes, so these files must arrive exactly as
# committed. Left to the rule above, the CRLF fixture is stored with its
# carriage returns stripped — it then tests nothing, while still looking
# like it does.
crates/vuwr-core/tests/corpus/** -text
examples/** -text
